Subject: stwo-cairo-prover: enable the wasm-bindgen getrandom backends (`js` / `wasm_js`) for wasm32 only

Why (Hellproof S2, wasm64): the prover crate turns on `getrandom/js` (0.2) and
`getrandom/wasm_js` (0.3) for every wasm target. In getrandom 0.2.17 the `js` feature also
covers wasm64 and takes precedence over the `custom` feature, so a wasm64 module built from the
monorepo imports wasm-bindgen glue (`__wbindgen_placeholder__::__wbg_getRandomValues_*`,
`__wbg_crypto_*`, `__wbindgen_object_drop_ref`, ...) that a host without the wasm-bindgen JS
runtime cannot satisfy; instantiation fails in Node and Chrome. wasm-bindgen's wasm64 support is
recent and its JS runtime is generated per module, so on wasm64 the embedder must provide a
`custom` backend (`register_custom_getrandom!` for 0.2, `--cfg getrandom_backend="custom"` for
0.3/0.4) instead. The CI wasm64 `cargo check` is unaffected either way.

Upstream: to be submitted as a PR against starkware-libs/proving (base cd7bc5f).

--- a/crates/prover/Cargo.toml
+++ b/crates/prover/Cargo.toml
@@ -42,8 +42,10 @@
 [target.'cfg(not(any(target_arch = "wasm32", target_arch = "wasm64")))'.dependencies]
 sonic-rs.workspace = true
 
-# Override getrandom feature flags for indirect dependencies.
-[target.'cfg(any(target_arch = "wasm32", target_arch = "wasm64"))'.dependencies]
+# Override getrandom feature flags for indirect dependencies. The `js` / `wasm_js` backends are
+# wasm-bindgen based: wasm32 only. On wasm64 the embedder supplies a `custom` backend
+# (`register_custom_getrandom!` for getrandom 0.2, `--cfg getrandom_backend="custom"` for 0.3).
+[target.'cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")'.dependencies]
 getrandom_v2.workspace = true
 getrandom_v3.workspace = true
 
